PROBLEM STATEMENT:
Two children, Lily and Ron, want to share a chocolate bar. Each square of the bar has an integer on it. Lily decides to share a contiguous segment of the bar such that:
The length of the segment equals Ron’s birth month m.
The sum of the integers in the segment equals Ron’s birth day d.
Determine how many ways Lily can divide the chocolate.
JAVA CODE:
import java.util.*;

class Result {
    public static int birthday(List<Integer> s, int d, int m) {
        int count = 0;
        // Iterate through possible starting points
        for (int i = 0; i <= s.size() - m; i++) {
            int sum = 0;
            // Sum the next m elements
            for (int j = 0; j < m; j++) {
                sum += s.get(i + j);
            }
            if (sum == d) {
                count++;
            }
        }
        return count;
    }
}

public class Solution {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);
        int n = sc.nextInt(); // number of squares
        List<Integer> s = new ArrayList<>();
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            s.add(sc.nextInt());
        }
        int d = sc.nextInt(); // Ron's birth day
        int m = sc.nextInt(); // Ron's birth month

        int result = Result.birthday(s, d, m);
        System.out.println(result);
    }
}
INPUT:
5
1 2 1 3 2
3 2
OUTPUT:
